{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3463","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3463","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3463\",\"parent_revision\":\"891a7cc8c6e466770bb086e954bd235f673386692e978bb6fbd19c7833172a58\",\"root_revision\":\"891a7cc8c6e466770bb086e954bd235f673386692e978bb6fbd19c7833172a58\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWithout it, \\\"tests are written against the architecture\\\" is a statement of intent that nothing enforces, and the drift it exists to prevent is invisible until someone reads both documents side by side.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Is Missing\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` now state that system and end-to-end tests are written against the architecture rather than against the code. Nothing makes that checkable. A test cannot declare which part of the specification it verifies, so:\\n\\n- a reader of a test cannot tell what design statement it defends;\\n- nobody can ask which parts of the architecture have no test at all;\\n- when an architecture statement changes, nothing identifies the tests that were resting on it.\\n\\nThe desired shape, as stated by the repository owner: an architecture document carries referenceable sections, and a test can say it verifies a named section.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Constraint That Decides Whether This Works\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**The identifiers must be stable, not positional.** A dotted numbering derived from position (`\u00a73.1.2.1`) is derived data: inserting a section renumbers its siblings and every reference to them, silently, exactly as the counts and line-anchored citations elsewhere in this repository did. The failure would be worse here because the references live in test files rather than prose.\\n\\nSo an identifier should be assigned once and never reused or recomputed \u2014 an opaque tag beside a human-readable heading, or an append-only number that is never renumbered when the document is reorganised. Whichever is chosen, reordering or rewording a section must not change its identifier.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What This Is Not\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis is not a return to tests that read prose. The deleted tests parsed a markdown document and asserted that code matched its wording \u2014 comparing two encodings of the same data. A test naming the section it covers asserts nothing about the document's text; it is metadata that makes coverage answerable in both directions. The distinction matters because the mechanisms look alike and the failure modes do not.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `plugins/development-harness/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `.claude/CLAUDE.md`'s \\\"Read the Architecture Before Changing the Design\\\".\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"cd1c2dc55afb39164c1c8c849a5cad4488b1871b17115e82660241afddff2fb8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUIyefw\"}"}